{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\23201\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Users\\\\23201\\\\.agents\\\\skills\\\\matlab-runner\\\\references\\\\mcp-readiness-ladder.md'; Get-Content -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Users\\\\23201\\\\.agents\\\\skills\\\\matlab-runner\\\\references\\\\failure-classes.md'\"","aggregated_output":"# MCP readiness ladder\r\n\r\nLoaded on demand by `matlab-runner`. The Agent does not need this table unless it is\r\nabout to claim MCP is ready �� which is exactly the claim that must not be made from\r\na config file.\r\n\r\n## A config check is not a readiness check\r\n\r\nA `sessionDetails.json` on disk, a listening PID, or a client entry in `.mcp.json`\r\nall look identical to a file-existence test and all prove nothing about whether a\r\ntool call will work. There are at least five distinct states, and only the fourth\r\nmeans \"usable\":\r\n\r\n| # | State | Looks fine? | Actually means |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| 1 | server process not running | yes | nothing is listening |\r\n| 2 | process running, wrong port | yes | the client will connect to the wrong thing |\r\n| 3 | handshake rejected | yes | auth or protocol mismatch |\r\n| 4 | handshake OK, `tools/call` fails | **yes** | the only state a config check cannot detect |\r\n\r\n## The ladder\r\n\r\nRun the staged probe and read its verdict, never a file listing:\r\n\r\n```powershell\r\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\\scripts\\Test-MatlabMcpExistingSession.ps1 -Json\r\n```\r\n\r\n| Stage | Check id | Level | Proves |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| 1 | `mcp.matlab-install` | L1 | MATLAB executable resolved, `VersionInfo.xml` readable |\r\n| 2 | `mcp.matlab-license` | L1 | license usable (SKIP by default, `-VerifyLicense` to force) |\r\n| 2 | `mcp.session-config` | L1 | session JSON parses, certificate exists, port valid |\r\n| 2 | `mcp.client-registration` | L2 | client args have no `display-mode`, `command` really exists |\r\n| 3 | `mcp.protocol-handshake` | L2 | TCP reachable and `initialize` returns a valid `result` |\r\n| 4 | `mcp.readonly-exec` | L3 | a read-only command really executed through `tools/call` |\r\n| 5 | `mcp.file-io` | L4 | token written to an isolated dir and read back identical |\r\n\r\n## Rules that must not be relaxed\r\n\r\n- **Only stage 4 passing upgrades `mcp.matlab-license` from SKIP to PASS**, and the\r\n  evidence (`provenBy = mcp.readonly-exec`) is recorded in `metrics`. A licence that\r\n  has merely not been tested is SKIP, never PASS.\r\n- **A failed stage makes every later stage SKIP** with reason \"upstream not passed\".\r\n  Never continue as if the earlier stage had succeeded �� this is how a broken\r\n  session produces a report full of unexplained later failures.\r\n- **An HTTP error must keep both the status code and the JSON-RPC error** in\r\n  `reason`. A bare `unauthorized` string hides the difference between \"the server\r\n  is down\" and \"the key is wrong\", which have opposite fixes.\r\n\r\n## Decision rule for this machine\r\n\r\n1. Prefer official MATLAB MCP auto mode, so the server reuses an existing shared\r\n   session or starts MATLAB automatically.\r\n2. Stay on MCP when the task needs repeated model edits, parameter sweeps with live\r\n   inspection, or anything user-visible on the desktop.\r\n3. Reserve `matlab -batch` for explicit requests: CI, headless smoke tests,\r\n   reproducible one-shot runs.\r\n4. If MCP is unavailable, **report the blocker**. Do not silently change execution\r\n   mode �� a batch rerun that succeeds hides the problem the user needs to see.\r\n\r\n## Setup\r\n\r\n```powershell\r\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\\scripts\\Setup-MatlabMcpExistingSession.ps1\r\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\\scripts\\Test-MatlabMcpExistingSession.ps1\r\n```\r\n\r\n## �Զ��򿪿ɼ� MATLAB ����\r\n\r\n�����вֿ�� `scripts/Start-MatlabDesktop.ps1`�����ȸ���ƥ������й�������ʱ��\r\n���洰�ڣ�û�� MATLAB ʱ�Զ��� Windows Shell �򿪿ɼ����棬�ȴ�����Ψһ\r\nreceipt�����ؽ��ٷ� stdio `auto` ���Ӳ�����ʵ����ִ����֤��\r\n�����δ����ʵ�����ȶ���������Ƿ��� `-NewSession` ���������ر��û�ԭ�Ự��\r\n`REUSED_EXISTING` ���������������� `newSessionVerified=true` ������ǰû��\r\nMATLAB ����ʱ�ſɼ�¼ `coldStartVerified=true`���˿ڡ�PID �� receipt ��������\r\n��������� MCP ִ����֤����� `docs/MATLAB_DESKTOP_STARTUP_ZH.md`��\r\n��Ҫ��ȷ�����ֶ����ʱ���� `-LaunchMode Shortcut`����ѡ���غ��ùٷ� MCP ִ��\r\n����ָ���� `mcpCodeFile`������ `-ConfirmReport` �˶Ի�ִ����ѡ�������������ɹ���\r\n����ʽ�� `-LaunchMode ComDesktop` �ɶ��� STA holder ������ע��Ŀɼ����沢���� COM ���ã�\r\n���� COM ���ؾ� PID ʱΪ `NOT_NEW`��������д���û��Ự��������������\r\nholder �����������ؽ��ٷ� stdio `auto` ����֤ʵ��ִ�У����������������˳��󸴺˳�����\r\n# Failure classes and what may be retried\r\n\r\nLoaded on demand by `matlab-runner`. Consult before retrying a failed run.\r\n\r\n## The table\r\n\r\n| Class | Auto-retry | Typical cause |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `TIMEOUT` | yes | process exceeded its budget and was killed |\r\n| `MCP_CONNECTION_ERROR` | yes | port closed, handshake rejected, bad API key |\r\n| `ENVIRONMENT_ERROR` | no | compiler or executable missing |\r\n| `LICENSE_ERROR` | no | product not licensed |\r\n| `VALIDATION_ERROR` | no | numeric or content mismatch |\r\n| `SIMULATION_ERROR` | no | solver error |\r\n| `CODEGEN_ERROR` | no | build error |\r\n| `MATLAB_RUNTIME_ERROR` | no | other runtime error |\r\n\r\n## Why classifying first is worth the effort\r\n\r\n- Retrying `LICENSE_ERROR` or `ENVIRONMENT_ERROR` cannot succeed. The second and\r\n  third attempts produce identical failures and burn the budget that a real fix\r\n  would have needed.\r\n- Retrying `VALIDATION_ERROR` is **worse than useless**: it converts a crisp\r\n  \"maxAbs 3.9e-01 exceeds tol 1e-06\" into a vague \"flaky\", and the number that\r\n  would have identified the bug is gone.\r\n- `TIMEOUT` and `MCP_CONNECTION_ERROR` are genuinely transient, so a bounded retry\r\n  is the right response �� provided the operation is idempotent.\r\n\r\n## Caps and the destructive-operation rule\r\n\r\nRetries are capped at **5 attempts**. Beyond that, stop and report: a fifth identical\r\nfailure is not a flake, and continuing hides it.\r\n\r\n**Non-idempotent or destructive operations �� downloads, installs, writes, deployments ��\r\nmust not be retried without explicit user approval.** The retry, not the first attempt,\r\nis what causes damage: a half-written file, a duplicated dataset, a partially applied\r\ninstall. When a retry would repeat a write, report and ask instead.\r\n\r\n## Distinguishing the three \"it ran but the answer is wrong\" cases\r\n\r\nThese are separate problems with separate fixes, and collapsing them into \"failed\"\r\nis how a real defect survives:\r\n\r\n| Symptom | Class | First thing to check |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| numbers differ from a golden value | `VALIDATION_ERROR` | the reference itself �� is it derived from the code under test? |\r\n| model/simulation aborts | `SIMULATION_ERROR` | solver settings, sample time, algebraic loops |\r\n| build fails after generation | `CODEGEN_ERROR` | unsupported construct; run `mas_codegen_ready` first |\r\n\r\nThe first row is the one worth internalising: a validation failure whose reference was\r\ncomputed by the code being validated is not a validation failure. That is how Phase 4's\r\nButterworth task reported PASS on a number that was 3.9 dB off.\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
